// REJECTS: Unexpected token '#{'. Valid alternatives: ['$[']
//
// A validation tree written with GraphFetchTree's `#{ ... }#` delimiters instead of
// DataQuality's `$[ ... ]$`. The two trees look identical inside -- property nodes, nested
// braces, `->subType(@Type)` downcasts -- and DataQuality's really is a graph-fetch tree in
// the protocol. But it is a SEPARATE grammar with its own delimiter tokens, and its
// `->subType(@` is its own SUBTYPE_START, not the GraphFetchTree one.
//
// This is the specific reuse a rewrite is invited to make: notice the trees are the same
// shape, route `validationTree:` at the existing graph-fetch parser, and inherit `#{ }#` as
// an accepted spelling. legend-engine does not accept it, and the alternative list here says
// so with a single-element set.
###DataQualityValidation
DataQualityValidation fixture::neg::GraphFetchDelimiters
{
   context: fromMappingAndRuntime(fixture::neg::M, fixture::neg::R);
   validationTree: #{ fixture::neg::Person { name } }#;
}
